  "_comment": "A turn with work in it: what the agent did, what it said, and what it stopped to ask. Sits beside examples.json rather than inside it because that file is a byte-identical lift and cannot be edited here. Every item carries an `audience` the readers no longer interpret; it goes when the field does. `turnEnd` stops the same turn where it stands: nobody answered the permission, so the request closes unanswered and the edit it was waiting on is left unfinished. Deliberately messy, because a tidy turn proves nothing: tools overlap and are revised out of the order they opened in, one title is longer than Slack will take on a task card and one detail is longer than the room left after it, a step is declined rather than failed, and the titles mix prose with the tool-call shape a host is as likely to emit — nothing produces these events yet, so the renderer has to survive both.",
